@module resolver
@lang aria
@version 0.1.0
@code_version git:fdea707
@aid_status reviewed
@aid_generated_by claude-opus-4-7
@aid_reviewed_by claude-opus-4-7
@layer 2
@aid_version 0.2
@purpose Two-pass name-resolution engine. Builds a scope hierarchy and registers declarations in pass 1; resolves every identifier use in pass 2 with error recovery and stdlib auto-suggestions.
@depends [parser, diagnostic]

---

@workflow resolve_pipeline
@purpose tokens + DeclIndex -> SymbolTable + Diagnostics
@steps
  1. init: new Resolver with empty SymbolTable + DiagnosticBag, pos = 0. [src: resolver.aria:28-40]
  2. universe_setup: push ScUniverse scope (scope 1), populate built-in types (i64, bool, str) and functions (print, panic, …). [src: resolver.aria:2580-2581, resolver.aria:202-350]
  3. module_setup: push ScModule scope (scope 2); scan for `use` decls and register imported modules as SkModule symbols. [src: resolver.aria:2584-2634]
  4. pass1: walk DeclIndex, register every top-level decl in module scope. fn -> SkFunction, type -> SkType, variants -> SkVariant, enum -> SkEnum, trait -> SkTrait, const -> SkConst. extern / fixture handled specially. [src: resolver.aria:2637, resolver.aria:398-518]
  5. pass2: walk DeclIndex again; for each decl with a body (fn / impl / const / entry / test), create a child scope and recursively resolve identifiers + bindings. [src: resolver.aria:2640, resolver.aria:580-647]
  6. Return ResolveResult (final SymbolTable + DiagnosticBag). [src: resolver.aria:2642]

---

@invariants
  Scope graph is a TREE — every Scope has exactly one parent (universe has parent=0); depth = parent.depth + 1. [src: scope.aria:99-100, scope.aria:115-125]
  lookup() walks the parent chain only — never sideways. [src: scope.aria:157-172]
  lookup_local() only checks the current scope. [src: scope.aria:142-154]
  Sentinel scope (id=0) and sentinel symbol (name="") mark missing entries; they are never surfaced to the user. [src: scope.aria:96-97, scope.aria:57-65]
  SkVariant is the ONLY symbol kind that may duplicate in a scope (qualified via Type.Variant at use site). Every other kind must be unique per scope. [src: resolver.aria:151-156]
  Builtin symbols live in the universe scope and never trigger shadowing warnings. [src: resolver.aria:172-175]
  Pass 1 must complete fully before pass 2 starts — bodies may forward-reference any top-level decl. [src: resolver.aria:401-402, resolver.aria:582-584]
  Multi-file bootstrap: all files in the same package share the universe + module scopes; per-token file info is preserved for diagnostics. [src: resolver.aria:2579-2584, resolver.aria:124-127]

---

@antipatterns
  Calling lookup() before universe/module scopes are initialised: every built-in resolves to missing. [src: resolver.aria:2580-2584]
  Mutating table / diagnostics in place instead of using _rset_* helpers: breaks the immutable-by-value invariant. [src: resolver.aria:92-120]
  Registering qualified method names (`Type_method`) as symbols: the checker owns those; the resolver must skip. [src: resolver.aria:1705-1721]
  Cross-file visibility checks: disabled by design in the multi-file bootstrap (all files treated as the same package). Do not re-enable without a module-boundary design. [src: resolver.aria:1686-1697]
  Resolving in a scope before its parent is created: parent-chain walk terminates prematurely. [src: scope.aria:157-172]

---

@fn resolve
@purpose Orchestrates two-pass resolution: populate builtins, scan use-decls, register top-level symbols, resolve bodies.
@pre tokens may be empty (EOF only); DeclIndex is built; all decls are registered in the index. [src: resolver.aria:2575]
@post ResolveResult with fully populated SymbolTable + all unresolved/duplicate/shadow diagnostics. [src: resolver.aria:2642]
@complexity O(N + M) where N = token count, M = decl count; lookup is O(D) where D = nesting depth (typically <= 20).
@thread_safety not-safe — Resolver is mutated in place across passes. [src: resolver.aria:15-26]
@antipatterns Do not re-call resolve() on the same tokens without resetting DeclIndex; do not edit tokens between passes.

---

@fn _pass1
@purpose Register every top-level decl (fns, types, consts, enums, traits) and their variants in module scope.
@pre universe + module scopes exist; DeclIndex populated. [src: resolver.aria:398]
@post Module scope populated; extern + fixture decls handled specially; variants registered as SkVariant. [src: resolver.aria:515-517]
@complexity O(M + K) where M = decls, K = variant count. [src: resolver.aria:398-518]
@thread_safety requires-sync — mutates r.table + r.diagnostics.
@antipatterns Registering impl methods or test helpers at top level — they belong inside their impl/test bodies. [src: resolver.aria:512-513]

---

@fn _pass2
@purpose Walk decl bodies and resolve every identifier use against the scope graph.
@pre Pass 1 complete; module scope has all top-level symbols; AST nodes in NodePool. [src: resolver.aria:580]
@post Every reachable identifier resolved or error-flagged; block/function scopes created; bindings registered. [src: resolver.aria:646-647]
@complexity O(M + B) where M = decls, B = total body size. [src: resolver.aria:580-647]
@thread_safety requires-sync — mutates r.table / r.diagnostics / r.current_scope.
@antipatterns Token-walking fallback for bodies where AST nodes exist: produces inconsistent resolution results — always use the AST path when available. [src: resolver.aria:598-614]

